# Code Style (Lint & Format)

## Tooling by language

| Stack | Linter | Formatter | Config files (sub-project repo root) |
|-------|--------|-----------|--------------------------------------|
| JS/TS (new) | Biome | Biome | `biome.json` |
| JS/TS (existing ESLint) | ESLint | Prettier | `eslint.config.*` + `prettier.config.*` |
| Python | Ruff | Ruff (`ruff format`) | `pyproject.toml` |

Do not put tool config in `.cursor/` — only rules and skills live there.

## Template defaults (new projects)

Copy from `templates/lint/` into the sub-project root. Default style:

| | JS/TS (Biome / Prettier) | Python (Ruff) |
|--|--------------------------|---------------|
| Indent | 2 spaces | 4 spaces |
| Quotes | single | single (format) |
| Semicolons | yes (JS/TS) | — |
| Line width | 100 | 88 |

Sub-projects may override via their own config files or `projects/<name>/.cursor/rules/`. Every sub-project must have linter + formatter config — no unconfigured repos.

## AI: before delivery (after code changes)

Work in `projects/<name>/` (or workspace root for template-only edits).

1. Detect stack: `biome.json` → Biome; `eslint.config.*` → ESLint + Prettier; `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.ruff]` → Ruff.
2. If `package.json` / `pyproject.toml` defines a **`lint` script that includes format check** → run that script first (`npm run lint`, etc.).
3. Otherwise run format then lint:
   - Biome: `npx @biomejs/biome format --write .` then `npx @biomejs/biome check .`
   - Prettier + ESLint: `npx prettier --write .` then `npm run lint` / `npx eslint .`
   - Ruff: `ruff format .` then `ruff check .`
4. Fix reported issues or explain blockers to the user.
5. Do not install pre-commit hooks unless the user asks; templates are optional.

See skill `code-style-workflow` for steps and copy commands.
